Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/runtime: mark frame pacer query result ASSERTED

vk_frame_pacer.c (added in upstream 6854f77017cf) stores the result of
GetQueryPoolResults() in a local that is only read by assert().  In a
release build NDEBUG compiles the assert out and MSVC raises C4189,
which mesa's meson.build promotes to an error with /we4189.  The
/wd4189 that meson adds for NDEBUG builds is only applied on the
GCC-syntax branch, so MSVC release builds fail:

  src/vulkan/runtime/vk_frame_pacer.c(132): error C4189: 'res': local
  variable is initialized but not referenced

Tag the variable ASSERTED, as the rest of src/vulkan/runtime does for
assert-only results.
---
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_frame_pacer.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_frame_pacer.c
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
 
       while (num_timestamps > 0) {
          /* Retrieve timestamp results from this queue. */
-         VkResult res = device->dispatch_table.GetQueryPoolResults(
+         ASSERTED VkResult res = device->dispatch_table.GetQueryPoolResults(
             _device, queue_ctx->queryPool, query_idx, num_timestamps,
             sizeof(struct query) * num_timestamps, &query_begin->gpu_ts, sizeof(struct query),
             VK_QUERY_RESULT_64_BIT);
